	(hierarchical_label "VOUT"
		(shape output)
		(at 152.4 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c7373598-4f07-406b-8f3a-a3dd9c75ef96")
	)
	(text "REVERSE-POLARITY PROTECTED, SOFT-START, SWITCHED DC INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9a98aa05-6f16-426b-b1f1-34fc66950058")
	)
	(text "19 V max in (SMBJ20A). Q1 = DMP4025LSD dual P-FET: unit A blocks reverse input, unit B is the switch.\nClose J2 (or bridge JP1) to turn on: R2 pulls GATE low, both FETs turn on, D1 limits |VGS| to 10 V.\nSwitch current < 0.5 mA. Open: R1 pulls GATE to VS and both FETs turn off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 41.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65b31ab3-5ff3-4747-a6f5-984e558159ff")
	)
	(text "SOFT START (C2 = Css)\nC2 feeds back VOUT to GATE through D3, so VOUT ramps at a fixed rate:\n  dV/dt ~ [(VIN - Vp)/R2 - Vp/R1] / C2,  Vp ~ 2.5-3 V (DMP4025LSD plateau, check on scope)\n  Inrush ~ C_load x dV/dt.  Ramp time ~ VIN / (dV/dt).\nWith R2 47k, R1 100k, C2 220nF into 680 uF:\n  12 V: ~0.8 V/ms, ~15 ms, ~0.55 A    19 V: ~1.5 V/ms, ~13 ms, ~1.0 A\nC2 100nF = ~2x faster/higher inrush; 470nF = ~2x slower/lower.\nD3 blocks the Miller path at turn-off (fast off, ~1 ms); R4 resets C2 (~0.2 s)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 127.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2d19c150-246a-4bda-9d56-3488f1323ad1")
	)
	(text "PROTECTION\nReverse input: Q1A body diode blocks; GATE ends up positive so both FETs stay off.\nD2 sits on VS, behind Q1A, so it never sees reverse polarity and F1 does not blow.\nSurge: Q1A body diode passes it to VS where D2 clamps (32.4 V at full pulse current).\nWrong adapter (> 22 V) will overload D2 and blow F1 - this circuit has no OV cut-off.\nQ1 VDS 40 V; VGS limited to 10 V by D1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 127.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60a1acc7-86b1-49a2-8235-19fb3ac8cf78")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT\nQ1: both drains (pins 5-8) carry full current - use copper pours.\nPins 1 and 3 (S1, S2) join on the PCB as VS.\nD2 close to Q1, short GND return. C2/D3/R4 close to Q1 pin 4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aec234b9-77f4-4fda-84c7-53ebc85c708b")
	)
